            <div xml:id="d592">

                <pb facs="0500" n="384" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg384"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 838.00/871.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Minister Smith.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 23.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-03-12">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 12, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department has received your No. 57,
                    of the 20th ultimo, in regard to the blockade of Cape Haitien by the Haitian
                    Government.</p>
                <p>In reply the Department desires to say that as your doubts that the blockade was
                    effective appear to be well founded, your action in not recognizing the blockade
                    is approved.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">John E. Osborne</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
